  "traps": [
    "composer.lock is left out: a Laravel lock pins about a hundred packages with source references and dist checksums and weighs some 300 KB, so every resolved is null",
    "two units share the root: the Composer app and the Vite asset build; package.json has no name, so that unit's name is null and it is referred to by its root",
    "\"php\": \"^8.2\" inside require is a platform requirement, a toolchain, not a package dependency",
    "artisan has no extension: it is PHP by its shebang",
    "welcome.blade.php is Blade, not PHP, although it ends in .php",
    "axios ships in the browser bundle but is declared in devDependencies: scope is dev as declared",
    "the PSR-4 root database/factories/ is declared in composer.json but the folder does not exist",
    "services come from .env.example, a template: the real .env is absent; Redis serves both cache and queue (QUEUE_CONNECTION, CACHE_STORE)",
    "phpunit.xml switches tests to SQLite in memory: an embedded engine, not an external service",
    "vendor/ is absent: composer.json post-autoload-dump runs project code (artisan package:discover) on install"
  ]
